      ],
      "text": "A point l in PT determines tautological L and rank-3 quotient L^perp whose fiber is C4/l; quotient not orthogonal complement. Cross-reference W036."
    },
    {
      "html_lines": [
        294,
        295
      ],
      "text": "Three displayed homogeneous quotient presentations; U1 weight+1 on l entails source weight -1/3 on quotient in determinant-one subgroup. W036 already preserves."
    },
    {
      "html_lines": [
        296,
        298
      ],
      "text": "Author's Hom equality has domain l⊕lperp, codomain printed S_R⊕S_L, and tensor form reverses spinor order S_L⊕S_R. A claimed one-generation role, not a complete dynamics result."
    },
    {
      "html_lines": [
        300,
        301
      ],
      "text": "Author prints (C_-1 ⊗ C3_(1/3)) ⊗ (C2_0 ⊕ C_-1 ⊕ C_+1). The FIRST connective is a tensor, although an algebraic repair could use a direct sum. Preserve literal tensor."
    },
    {
      "html_lines": [
        303,
        306
      ],
      "text": "Author next prints six weighted terms with first three ⊕ separators, last two + separators. Do not normalize literal symbol order."
    },
    {
      "html_lines": [
        306,
        310
      ],
      "text": "Author assigns six first-generation roles in order, including a right-handed neutrino; interpretation as source assertion not verified Standard Model dynamics."
    },
    {
      "html_lines": [
        311,
        311
      ],
      "text": "Source explicitly distinguishes its proposal from placing all gauge groups into one GUT Lie group; already covered by W038."
    }
